# Project Organization

- This repo is a compact Vercel Express API project. Keep runtime API code under `api/` because `tsconfig.json` includes `api/**/*.ts`.
- `api/index.ts` owns the exported Express app and route mounting. Keep route files under `api/routes/`.
- `api/db.ts` is the single Mongo connection helper. Reuse it instead of opening new Mongoose connections.
- Use focused folders for new API code: `api/middleware`, `api/models`, `api/services`, `api/utils`, and `api/validation`.
- Keep operational scripts under `scripts/`; run them with the package scripts so `.env` loading stays consistent.
- Keep architecture notes and implementation plans under `docs/`; do not mix docs-only flow descriptions with runtime code.
- Avoid broad restructuring unless the user asks for it. Prefer small modules that match the current layout.
